The Look of Silence (Indonesian: Senyap, "Silence") is a 2014 internationally co-produced documentary
film directed by Joshua Oppenheimer about the Indonesian mass killings of 1965–66.

10
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
The film is a companion piece to his 2012 documentary The Act of Killing.

11
01:18:34,285 --> 01:18:40,285
Executive producers were Werner Herzog, Errol Morris, and Andre Singer.

12
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It was nominated for the Academy Award for Best
Documentary Feature at the 88th Academy Awards.

13
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
The film explores themes of loss of loved one, mass
murder, biography, indonesia, torture.
